  "rebuild_gaps": [
    "The RinkSpace OneDrive project contains its integration wrappers and a byte-preserved standalone ViTPose-H helper, but not complete GVHMR/PyTorch3D source trees, external package installations or model files.",
    "GVHMR has three current tracked local modifications. Their paths, hashes and a source-only patch against the exact Git HEAD are preserved; applying the patch to an independent clean clone and full runtime validation remain undone.",
    "The external run_vitpose_h.py helper is byte-preserved in source_helpers with provenance; observations.py still defaults to the sibling path. Author/license and public redistribution permission are unknown.",
    "body_prior.py checks the exact FSrotation interpreter prefix and changes cwd to its external GVHMR root. observations.py and bootstrap.py retain external absolute or sibling paths. No path refactor was made.",
    "Current CUDA package versions differ from the frozen upstream GVHMR requirements (which name Python 3.10, torch 2.3.0+cu121 and a Linux PyTorch3D wheel). Neither recipe is a verified portable Windows rebuild of the current runtime.",
    "GTSAM native build.bat references separate Data vendor headers/import libraries and hardcoded MSVC/conda paths. environment.yml alone does not supply the complete build toolchain.",
    "Model byte identity records and download links do not establish redistribution rights. Exact model licenses, embedded upstream component notices and the project owner license selection remain separate public-release questions."
  ],
